# Generated by the harness at run time. Both carry repo paths, timings and
# verdicts, and neither is an input to anything, so a clone must not track
# them. Previously ignored only via .git/info/exclude, which is local to one
# machine: a fresh clone would have offered them for commit.
.claude/harness-ledger.jsonl
.claude/optimise-cycle-report.md

# Fix round 3, finding 1 (specs/record-fixed-findings.md): conduct-plan's
# cross-round prior_findings state. Carries every open finding's location
# and claim VERBATIM -- exactly the free text the ledger schema itself is
# designed to keep out (AC-SEC-2, "no free text, ever"), and exactly the
# class of content (a quoted source line, a hardcoded secret a lens
# happened to flag) that must never reach a commit on a public repository.
# Route B's join (specs/record-fixed-findings.md) requires this data to
# survive between ticks; it must never survive inside a TRACKED file.
.claude/conductor-prior-findings.json

# Python bytecode cache. test/destructive-git-guard.test.js's M3 allowlist
# parity check imports hooks/destructive-git-guard.py as a module (to read
# its GIT_ENV_ALLOWLIST constant as real data, not scraped source text),
# which makes CPython write this on every run.
hooks/__pycache__/
